riddle_english:
It comes on shoulders, it goes on shoulders;
Though innocent, it gets beaten.
At worship and festivals, I am called upon;
Grand celebration is my life.

You play me with two hands;
To my rhythm, the heart begins to dance.
Grand celebration is my life.

Pieces move across the board;
The king stays in the middle.
The battle is fought with the strength of the mind;
No field is needed for it.

Two languages were tied inside one state;
Ahmedabad’s streets counted student footsteps.
“Chacha’s” voice travelled from village to village;
on the first of May the knot came undone—which movement was this?

riddle_original:
સવારના અંધારામાં કેન આવે, ચરબી માપાય ને પાવતી મળે;
વર્ષ પૂરું થાય ત્યારે ભાવફેરનો હિસાબ ગામમાં પાછો ફરે.
ઢોર વધુ હોય તેને મત વધુ નહીં—દર સભ્યનો એક મત;
ખેડા-આણંદની આ નાની લોકશાળા કઈ?

riddle_english:
Before sunrise the milk can arrives, fat is tested and a slip is issued;
at year’s end the price difference returns to the village.
Owning more cattle brings no extra vote—each member has one;
what is this small school of democracy in Kheda and Anand?

riddle_original:
હોળીના દિવસો, ગામના પાદરે બે ટોળાં;
લાકડીનો છેડો વાંકો, દડો ચીંથરાનો કે લાકડાનો.
જાળીવાળો ગોલ નહીં—કાંડાનું બળ ને ભાગોળનો દાવ;
આ તળપદી રમત કઈ?

riddle_english:
Around Holi, two groups meet on the village outskirts;
a stick bends at one end and the ball may be tightly wound cloth or wood.
There is no netted goal—only strong wrists and the open boundary land;
which folk game is this?

riddle_original:
પાંચ નાનાં કૂકા, એક આકાશે જાય;
એ નીચે આવે એ પહેલાં જમીનવાળાં હાથમાં ભેગાં.
એકથી બે, બેમાંથી વધુ—આંગળીઓનું ગણિત;
ઓટલે રમાતી આ રમત કઈ?

riddle_english:
My opponent is not on the ground but in the sky;
one hand holds the reel while the other gives life to the string.
When two lines meet the rooftop falls silent;
when one is cut the whole street shouts—what contest is this?

It asks, “How far?” and a lamp burns in reply;
if the lamp goes out, the road ends too.
With which line does this well-known rhyme of Gujarati childhood begin?

Chaki brought a grain of rice and Chako brought a mung bean;
khichdi was cooked, and then the whole tale became tangled.
Which pair of birds belongs to this well-known Gujarati children’s folktale?

riddle_original:
Namaku juga dikenali sebagai negeri,
Yang membawa gelaran Darul Ta’zim;
Apakah negeri yang dimaksudkan ini?

riddle_english:
My name is also known as a state,
Which bears the title Darul Ta’zim;
Which state is being referred to?

This game is a year-round pastime for children to pass the time while bathing; 
it’s played in the morning or evening, and Sundays are usually very crowded because 
many children gather at the river to bathe or just to play. What is this game?

riddle_original:
Tí wọ́n bá ń hó Ègbá ẹ́dide o!
orúkọ mi kì í gbẹ́yìn bẹ́ẹ̀;
Èmi ni ìgúnnugún tí ń dẹ́rù ba àwọn Ìlàrí Ọ̀yọ́.

riddle_english:
Wherever they chant the uprising of the Egba people,
my name is never forgotten;
I am a thorn in the flesh of the Oyo Empire’s tax collectors.

There is a town with twelve houses; 
only two people live there, 
they feed each other and eat each other.

riddle_original:
Tí mo bá ń lọ, 
ó ń tẹ̀ lé mi; 
tí mo bá dúró, ó dúró; 
bẹ́ẹ̀ ni n kò leè mú un.

riddle_english:
When I go, 
it follows me; 
when I stop, it stops; 
yet I cannot wrestle it to the ground or catch it.
